/-!
# The physical `L¹ ∩ L²` realization of the finite `Q4` multiplier

The finite-radius calculation in the paper is made first with literal
convolution kernels and only then read as an `L²` `TT*` identity.  The
completed Fourier multiplier in `Q4FiniteRadiusOperators` is therefore not
used as a replacement definition for physical convolution here.  Instead we
prove that, on an explicit `L¹ ∩ L²` carrier, its representative agrees
almost everywhere with the convolution by the compact Schwartz kernel.

The proof is the standard argument from the paper in a form suitable for the
finite product: Fubini gives the Fourier transform of the literal
convolution; multiplication by the Schwartz symbol is then compared with the
`L²` multiplier through tempered distributions.  Finally distributional
uniqueness for locally integrable functions gives the asserted a.e. identity.
-/

